# Review: BookmarksPlugin

The plugin implements every feature the spec names: the `Bookmark` type with its label and icon
annotations, `AddFromSnapshot` and `Summarize` operations, the plugin-crx page action, article and
card surfaces, and unanchored comments. The snapshot mapping is well tested in `Bookmark.test.ts`,
and the surfaces have stories. Nothing exercises the operations themselves, the page-action
contribution or the comment config, so most behavioural items are `untested`.

The one real divergence is the excerpt rule: `Bookmark.fromSnapshot` prefers `selection.text` over
`hints.ogDescription`, the reverse of F-2.1 and of the `Bookmark` type comment; the tests pin the
code's order. The page action also adds a third context (`picker`) the spec does not list.

Of 20 items: 7 done, 7 untested, 0 partial, 2 diverged, 4 missing.

