```mdl
verdict F-2.1: AddFromSnapshot creates the Bookmark and returns its id, but the excerpt prefers the selection over ogDescription.
  status: diverged
  evidence: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-bookmarks/src/types/BookmarkOperation.ts#AddFromSnapshot, github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-bookmarks/src/operations/add-from-snapshot.ts, github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-bookmarks/src/types/Bookmark.ts#fromSnapshot]
  tests: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-bookmarks/src/types/Bookmark.test.ts]
  walkthrough:
    - The operation declares `{ snapshot, target }` in and `{ id }` out. github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-bookmarks/src/types/BookmarkOperation.ts#AddFromSnapshot
    - fromSnapshot maps the snapshot fields onto a new Bookmark. github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-bookmarks/src/types/Bookmark.ts#fromSnapshot
    - The handler adds the object through SpaceOperation.AddObject on the target's space and returns its id. github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-bookmarks/src/operations/add-from-snapshot.ts
  note: |
    `fromSnapshot` computes `excerpt` as `selection.text.slice(0, 280) ?? hints.ogDescription`, the reverse of the spec's
    `ogDescription ?? selection`. The code comment and the test "excerpt prefers the picked/selected text over
    og:description" make this deliberate, so the spec is stale. The handler writes via `SpaceOperation.AddObject`
    (by `target.spaceId`), not straight into `target`.
```

